ranch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ie1a176e74473267cefcdd28bb7cc379f2230b763" commit="807e93ed2e9a9752e61e78ebdd0b26dfb5cd38bc" commit_message="CHROMIUM: net: wireless: bcmdhd: do not save btcoex state in statics  Instead of using static variables to save device state allocate memory for it in per-device structure.  Remove ts_dhcp_start, ts_dhcp_ok, and dhcp_done members from per-device state as they are not used.  Remove externs guarded by #ifdef PKT_FILTER_SUPPORT as they are not used either.  BUG=None TEST=Build and boot Ryu, use Wifi and Bluetooth.  Change-Id: Ie1a176e74473267cefcdd28bb7cc379f2230b763 Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/312969 Reviewed-by: Dmitry Shmidt &lt;dimitrysh@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="312969" owner_email="dtor@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/69/312969/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Id3fa805a666ced54e09b4ff8f0d69efadec543f7" commit="2f74b958a51a064a501b4eda7a65d84246e425ed" commit_message="CHROMIUM: net: wireless: bcmdhd: tighten up parsing BTCOEXMODE command  Move all ugliness of command parsing and response formatting from wl_cfg80211_set_btcoex_dhcp() into wl_android_priv_cmd() and make sure that length of &quot;BTCOEXMODE&quot; command is enough, before using the position where target mode is supposedly encoded.  BUG=None TEST=Build and boot Ryu, use Wifi and Bluetooth.  Change-Id: Id3fa805a666ced54e09b4ff8f0d69efadec543f7 Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/313010 Reviewed-by: Dmitry Shmidt &lt;dimitrysh@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="313010" owner_email="dtor@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kern