t we want to run on different machines and CPU models. This coverage should be restored at a future time.  BUG=chromium:538759 TEST=test_that -b wolf platform_DebugDaemonGetPerfData  Change-Id: I716853492ac1f1f557578dbc1630728e53ddca46 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/313206 Commit-Ready: David Sharp &lt;dhsharp@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Sharp &lt;dhsharp@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Simon Que &lt;sque@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="313206" owner_email="dhsharp@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/06/313206/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia2a7edb577350cd4aa1c9835f24f4e3df2e508e2" commit="9f1a071c17538f705769b37b30f4ce2863dfbcce" commit_message="flash_ec: Accomodate using flashrom on beaglebone  Currently, using flash_ec for mec1322 chips only supports flashing from servo v2.  Updated to work from v3 as well.  This is a resubmission.  BUG=chromium:554230 BRANCH=None TEST=tested locally with beaglebone/cyan setup at my desk      Ran flash_ec --board=cyan --chip=mec1322      --image=/tmp/image.bin.  Also ran with servov2.  Change-Id: Ia2a7edb577350cd4aa1c9835f24f4e3df2e508e2 Signed-off-by: Shelley Chen &lt;shchen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/313053 Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="313053" owner_email="shchen@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/53/313053/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I94a1072084618988df52b40ffb90d35418c55336" commit="f81dc705c3f923848508fb346cb43d84e6596f55" commit_message="CHROMIUM: i2c: tegra: Disable interrupts for sending packets  Disable interrupts while sending the packet header and payload. This prevents the possibility of getting interrupted between the header and the payload being written to the TX FIFO.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46922 TEST=run AuptTest and look for timeouts  Change-Id: I94a1072084618988df52b40ffb90d35418c55336 Signed-off-by: Rhyland Klein &lt;rklein@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/312530 Commit-Ready: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="312530" owner_email="rklein@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/30/312530/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I6df071ccb08f39c5fae84190c4f2725d5d2280ba" commit="aab0eb68554de1d7553ad5cb787636a75ac9f6c1" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/nouveau: Avoid kernel mutex locking mesg  Move mutex locking outside of rcu_read_lock, avoids kernel mesg  [   63.021218] BUG: sleeping function called from invalid context at kernel/locking/mutex.c:615 [   63.030153] in_atomic(): 0, irqs_disabled(): 0, pid: 926, name: nouveau_pushbuf [   63.037741] INFO: lockdep is turned off. [   63.041700] Preemption disabled at:[&lt;ffffffc000abe338&gt;] printk+0x6c/0x78  Change-Id: I6df071ccb08f39c5fae84190c4f2725d5d2280ba Signed-off-by: David Ung &lt;davidu@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/312751 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="312751" owner_email="davidu@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/51/312751/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id984b63f8c0c2d5c042265fd86b3d0c71fd68e6f" commit="8ad1109f87894cc9345b4ed4dc4fa4bd5cb0043c" commit_message="snoball: Correct DMA UART channels  Snoball uses DMA2 + DMA3 for UART1 debug console. No changes are needed to STM32_SYSCFG_CFGR1 since this is the register default config.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47851 BRANCH=None TEST=Boot snoball, verify EC console works in both directions.  Signed-off-by: Shawn Nematbakhsh &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: Id984b63f8c0c2d5c042265fd86b3d0c71fd68e6f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/313168 Commit-Ready: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alec Berg &lt;alecaberg@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="313168" owner_email="shawnn@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/68/313168/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I77993ef30275bf84567ee0a9f04298b5fac94e04" commit="8181d4c3f81cea0d1371fdb70892fbdab92ca956" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/tegra: Fix wrong plane-&gt;crtc dereference  There is a kernel NULL pointer crash after this patch is merged: &quot;4de84b63c1d8 UPSTREAM: drm/atomic: fix out of bounds read in for_each_*_in_state helpers&quot;  The reason for that is, in tegra drm driver, we deference the wrong &quot;plane-&gt;crtc&quot;. The crtc in an atomic commit is in &quot;plane_state-&gt;crtc&quot;. So this patch fixes this crash.  The reason why we didn't hit the crash before is, before apply that upstream patch, in tegra_dc_evaluate_bandwidth, we have:  if (!crtc_state)  break;  And this avoids calling tegra_dc_calculate_bandwidth which triggers the crash. The upstream patch fixes the issue which crtc_state in a &quot;f